WEBVTT

00:10.360 --> 00:12.560
Paradorn.

00:12.640 --> 00:14.840
Paradorn.

00:14.920 --> 00:16.880
Paradorn.

00:18.480 --> 00:22.520
They say power changes people.

00:23.280 --> 00:26.920
Or maybe it simply rips off the mask

00:27.000 --> 00:28.720
and reveals

00:29.480 --> 00:31.440
who they really are.

01:35.200 --> 01:38.680
1 MONTH BEFORE THE ELECTION

01:41.680 --> 01:43.800
Has anyone ever wondered, like I have,

01:44.560 --> 01:45.560
why…

01:46.080 --> 01:48.160
whenever we talk about change,

01:48.800 --> 01:53.400
adults always say that change takes time?

01:54.720 --> 01:55.760
How many years?

01:55.840 --> 01:56.920
Three years?

01:57.440 --> 01:58.480
Five years?

01:58.560 --> 02:02.320
Sometimes, I'm no longer sure

02:02.880 --> 02:04.640
whether it's a real reason

02:05.200 --> 02:07.400
or just an excuse to do nothing at all.

02:09.560 --> 02:10.600
Yes!

02:10.680 --> 02:11.720
-You're right.
-Yes!

02:11.800 --> 02:14.920
I'm not saying that change is easy.

02:16.160 --> 02:17.640
But my point is

02:18.560 --> 02:20.600
that if we start
by doing just one thing at a time,

02:21.560 --> 02:24.240
we'll only see one result at a time.

02:26.200 --> 02:28.760
But if we start
by doing 100 things at once,

02:30.680 --> 02:33.040
the progress of 100 years

02:33.560 --> 02:36.120
might happen within a single year.

02:36.640 --> 02:37.480
Right?

02:37.560 --> 02:38.560
Right!

02:45.200 --> 02:49.440
Paradorn.

02:49.520 --> 02:54.120
Paradorn.

03:05.160 --> 03:06.720
Hello.

03:06.800 --> 03:08.400
I'm Nanno, Number 2,

03:11.120 --> 03:13.240
here with a policy…

03:16.600 --> 03:18.600
What policy should I go with?

03:20.360 --> 03:21.280
Oh.

03:21.800 --> 03:24.040
"New student, new life," then.

03:25.040 --> 03:28.560
Anyway, please take care of me,

03:29.600 --> 03:31.560
and my heart too.

03:35.280 --> 03:37.280
I just applied recently,

03:37.800 --> 03:40.120
so I didn't really prepare any policies.

03:40.200 --> 03:41.960
But that's okay, right?

03:42.480 --> 03:44.240
I'd rather hear ideas from everyone.

03:52.040 --> 03:55.000
Did she copy our idea?
She just changed the wording.

03:55.080 --> 03:57.440
I'm ready to kiss everyone now.

04:17.280 --> 04:18.240
Hey!

04:18.320 --> 04:20.400
-Me first!
-Me first!

04:20.480 --> 04:21.920
Hurry up.

04:22.000 --> 04:24.400
Go, go. Hurry.

04:24.480 --> 04:26.600
The line is long now.

04:28.120 --> 04:30.320
Wow.

04:49.240 --> 04:51.880
I'm Nanno, No. 2. Please support me.

04:52.600 --> 04:53.440
Sure.

05:02.720 --> 05:04.760
I really like your idea.

05:10.240 --> 05:11.960
So I'd like to…

05:17.840 --> 05:19.320
share some ideas too.

05:21.520 --> 05:23.120
If it's you,

05:23.640 --> 05:25.480
I can give you two kisses.

05:28.440 --> 05:29.440
No need.

05:31.000 --> 05:34.720
I'm here to exchange ideas
for the benefit of the school,

05:35.480 --> 05:37.320
not for personal gain.

05:56.520 --> 06:00.360
Hmm… whose is this?
Looks familiar, doesn't it?

06:00.440 --> 06:06.240
-Whoa.
-Boo!

06:06.320 --> 06:07.440
Just throw it away.

06:15.160 --> 06:17.720
Distribute the budget to each class rep

06:17.800 --> 06:19.760
and let them manage it

06:19.840 --> 06:21.480
and set their own rules.

06:21.560 --> 06:24.320
Do they think
everyone has that much free time?

06:24.840 --> 06:26.480
No. No one's free.

06:26.560 --> 06:29.800
Why give class reps more work?

06:29.880 --> 06:32.520
-Yeah, that's true.
-Why?

06:34.040 --> 06:35.760
Yeah!

06:59.840 --> 07:01.680
The latest poll results are out.

07:01.760 --> 07:02.600
Really?

07:04.520 --> 07:05.400
How is it?

07:06.280 --> 07:09.000
Can our 100 policies compete
with Nanno's single kiss?

07:13.040 --> 07:16.200
Honestly, Nanno's initial momentum
was very concerning.

07:16.280 --> 07:18.320
But based on the current poll,
it's clear that

07:18.400 --> 07:21.680
even though she created buzz,
it doesn't mean people will vote for her.

07:21.760 --> 07:23.840
Because most people can still tell

07:23.920 --> 07:26.280
who's real
and who's just chasing attention.

07:27.000 --> 07:27.960
Right?

07:28.040 --> 07:29.920
And from further surveys,

07:30.000 --> 07:33.560
people are interested in the policy
of decentralizing power to class reps.

07:33.640 --> 07:36.760
If we can push this
as our flagship policy,

07:36.840 --> 07:39.200
we'll gain more support from voters.

07:40.280 --> 07:42.040
As for Nanno,

07:42.880 --> 07:46.760
just let her bury herself
with her past scandals.

07:49.640 --> 07:50.600
-Shit.
-Shit.

07:50.680 --> 07:52.880
-Is that real?
-Is that Nanno?

07:52.960 --> 07:54.880
-Who uploaded this?
-Zoom in.

07:55.480 --> 07:56.480
It's so clear.

07:57.680 --> 07:59.880
Nanno's popularity
is definitely going to drop.

07:59.960 --> 08:00.840
Easy for us.

08:01.360 --> 08:03.800
Damn, look at this.

08:03.880 --> 08:05.600
Did she really do it?

08:05.680 --> 08:07.320
Shit.

08:07.400 --> 08:09.360
-Did you see it?
-Student body president?

08:10.080 --> 08:11.440
Did you see your friend yet?

08:11.520 --> 08:12.640
Where?

08:26.560 --> 08:28.400
-Shit, how is this possible?
-Damn.

08:28.480 --> 08:31.520
-Whoa. Shit.
-What?

08:31.600 --> 08:34.320
-Shit. Is that real?
-Damn.

08:51.120 --> 08:54.400
Regarding the controversy about me…

09:00.360 --> 09:02.240
I'd like to confirm

09:02.840 --> 09:04.600
that everything you've seen

09:06.400 --> 09:07.280
is true.

09:07.360 --> 09:09.000
-What?
-Shit.

09:09.080 --> 09:10.800
Damn.

09:10.880 --> 09:13.160
Is that real? Shit.

09:13.240 --> 09:14.120
Gosh.

09:19.080 --> 09:20.600
Just kidding.

09:35.680 --> 09:39.800
These days, anyone can easily fall victim
to something like this.

09:43.120 --> 09:43.960
Shit.

09:44.960 --> 09:46.400
Hey, isn't that a campaign group?

09:47.360 --> 09:48.280
Are they friends?

09:48.360 --> 09:49.560
Yeah, right?

09:49.640 --> 09:50.840
Paradorn, right?

09:50.920 --> 09:52.360
-Paradorn?
-Yeah.

09:53.080 --> 09:54.960
No matter how real it looks,

09:56.120 --> 09:57.680
fake…

09:58.480 --> 09:59.680
is still fake.

10:03.040 --> 10:05.120
And the one who should be punished

10:05.200 --> 10:09.600
is the person who created the fake content
and used it to ruin someone else's life.

10:10.440 --> 10:12.440
Let me give you a hint.

10:12.960 --> 10:14.840
The one who benefits from this

10:16.280 --> 10:17.920
is the one who did it.

10:21.600 --> 10:23.520
-That's playing dirty.
-Yeah.

10:23.600 --> 10:26.720
-Yes.
-That's right!

10:28.280 --> 10:30.920
-Playing dirty.
-Yes!

10:31.000 --> 10:32.240
Yes.

10:32.320 --> 10:33.760
How is that even possible?

10:34.280 --> 10:35.760
She just acts slutty all day.

10:35.840 --> 10:38.440
The real issue is
that people misunderstood

10:38.520 --> 10:40.120
and think we did something dirty

10:40.200 --> 10:43.520
to damage her reputation,
so she's gaining sympathy votes.

10:43.600 --> 10:46.040
On election day,
we have to vote for Nanno.

10:46.120 --> 10:47.000
Yeah!

10:47.080 --> 10:49.120
So we can stand against patriarchy.

10:49.200 --> 10:53.240
Nanno! Nanno!

10:53.320 --> 10:54.760
So stupid.

10:56.960 --> 10:58.280
But did we actually do it?

10:59.680 --> 11:00.880
What do you mean?

11:00.960 --> 11:03.280
Nanno! Nanno!

11:03.360 --> 11:05.080
Didn't I already tell you guys?

11:06.040 --> 11:08.960
The clip was already uploaded.
I just shared it.

11:09.040 --> 11:14.400
Nanno! Nanno!

11:14.480 --> 11:17.160
But you were the first one
who saw it, right?

11:17.240 --> 11:19.800
Why would I go out of my way
to sabotage her?

11:21.360 --> 11:23.680
We're already leading in the polls.
You saw that yourself.

11:24.200 --> 11:26.120
She's not even on my radar.

11:26.200 --> 11:28.240
Didn't Nanno say it herself?

11:28.320 --> 11:31.520
The one who benefits from this
is the one who released the clip.

11:32.160 --> 11:34.080
You all saw who benefits the most.

11:34.160 --> 11:35.280
Hey!

11:38.000 --> 11:39.800
Stop fighting each other.

11:41.160 --> 11:42.800
Polls are just numbers.

11:43.400 --> 11:44.600
POPULARITY POLL
PARADORN, NANNO

11:44.680 --> 11:47.640
Even if those numbers say we're losing.

11:47.720 --> 11:48.720
Hello.

11:48.800 --> 11:50.280
-Nanno.
-Thank you.

11:50.360 --> 11:53.240
Then we have to come up with more policies
and finish them tonight,

11:53.320 --> 11:55.680
so we can continue the campaign tomorrow.

11:55.760 --> 11:57.800
We have hundreds of policies.
What else do you want?

11:57.880 --> 12:00.280
Even if it's thousands,
you still have to think of something.

12:00.360 --> 12:02.080
Whether it works or not, who cares.

12:02.160 --> 12:05.800
Hey. If that's the case, Paradorn won't be
different from the previous president,

12:06.400 --> 12:08.400
making promises he can't keep.

12:15.080 --> 12:17.640
-Please vote for Nanno.
-Number 2.

12:17.720 --> 12:19.920
-Nanno! Nanno!
-Please support Number 2, Nanno.

12:20.000 --> 12:21.360
Please vote for Number 2.

12:21.440 --> 12:23.760
-Vote for Number 2.
-Don't forget to vote for Nanno.

12:23.840 --> 12:27.680
Nanno! Nanno!

12:28.520 --> 12:29.480
Hey!

12:41.080 --> 12:42.080
You know,

12:43.680 --> 12:45.640
I've been preparing since last year

12:46.160 --> 12:48.000
for this year's
student body president election.

12:49.280 --> 12:51.600
I've been brainstorming policies
with the team nonstop.

12:51.680 --> 12:52.840
But you…

12:55.680 --> 12:57.880
You didn't even seem prepared at all.

13:01.560 --> 13:05.040
And look at you now.
You're even more popular than me.

13:06.280 --> 13:07.520
How did you do it?

13:08.880 --> 13:10.000
Yeah.

13:10.520 --> 13:11.960
How do you think?

13:19.400 --> 13:20.800
I misunderstood.

13:22.440 --> 13:26.800
I thought people would choose a leader
based on reason and facts.

13:28.480 --> 13:30.280
But in reality, that's not the case.

13:31.320 --> 13:34.120
You're really serious
about this election, aren't you?

13:36.440 --> 13:37.960
Because this is my first step.

13:39.720 --> 13:42.640
The first step to changing something.

13:43.600 --> 13:45.200
Starting from this school,

13:46.720 --> 13:48.960
so that in the future,

13:49.600 --> 13:52.840
I might have a chance
to change society for the better.

13:54.600 --> 13:56.240
Better how?

13:58.160 --> 14:00.200
The way you want it to be?

14:08.480 --> 14:10.800
But there are still three days left.

14:10.880 --> 14:12.840
Anything can happen, right?

14:23.760 --> 14:24.640
Hey!

14:32.480 --> 14:33.720
Shit.

14:33.800 --> 14:35.080
Oh.

14:35.760 --> 14:36.720
Hey.

14:36.800 --> 14:39.000
-Does it hurt?
-Oh.

14:39.520 --> 14:40.760
That's bad.

14:41.280 --> 14:43.360
SUPERHERO!

14:44.280 --> 14:45.480
Please don't get up yet.

14:46.000 --> 14:48.760
Easy.

14:48.840 --> 14:50.320
I THOUGHT HE WAS SUPERMAN

14:50.400 --> 14:52.760
Are you okay? Take it easy.

14:52.840 --> 14:53.680
Is he okay?

14:53.760 --> 14:54.720
Are you all right?

14:55.680 --> 14:57.560
Damn, that was so cool.

14:58.360 --> 14:59.240
Are you all right?

14:59.320 --> 15:02.920
Wow, that's straight out
of a Korean drama.

15:03.000 --> 15:04.480
Such a gentleman.

15:04.560 --> 15:06.640
THE REAL HERO

15:06.720 --> 15:08.840
I'LL VOTE FOR HIM

15:08.920 --> 15:09.840
NO NEED FOR AN ELECTION. CROWN HIM.

15:09.920 --> 15:10.960
WE NEED SMART CROSSWALK PROJECT!

15:11.040 --> 15:12.400
VOTE NUMBER 1

15:13.360 --> 15:16.520
ELECTION DAY

15:16.600 --> 15:18.400
BALLOT FOR THE 66TH STUDENT BODY PRESIDENT

15:18.480 --> 15:19.600
CANDIDATE NUMBER

15:45.560 --> 15:51.120
CONGRATULATIONS TO MR. PARADORN
THE 66TH STUDENT BODY PRESIDENT

15:57.480 --> 15:59.040
Congratulations, Paradorn.

16:04.360 --> 16:05.480
Thanks, Nanno.

17:05.840 --> 17:07.120
Hey, hurry up.

17:09.520 --> 17:12.200
Take these three boxes out
and replace them.

17:33.600 --> 17:34.640
What the hell?

17:35.400 --> 17:36.440
Shit!

17:38.800 --> 17:40.400
What the hell did you do, New?

17:40.480 --> 17:41.600
Do you even realize?!

17:43.280 --> 17:45.040
Damn. I might have already won.

17:45.120 --> 17:46.280
Damn it.

17:46.360 --> 17:47.360
Damn.

17:47.440 --> 17:48.440
Damn you.

17:48.960 --> 17:51.560
You're really working hard
at being an idiot.

17:58.160 --> 17:59.160
I…

18:00.120 --> 18:01.880
Paradorn Tangnaitham,

18:03.200 --> 18:05.120
the 66th student body president,

18:06.280 --> 18:11.040
have discovered that there was fraud
in this election.

18:12.600 --> 18:16.320
The one responsible
is one of my own party members.

18:42.120 --> 18:44.120
I was the one
who replaced all the ballot boxes

18:45.960 --> 18:48.000
to ensure Paradorn's victory.

18:48.520 --> 18:49.360
-What?
-What the fuck?

18:49.440 --> 18:51.400
-Just get out.
-Why would you do that?

18:51.480 --> 18:53.320
-Go home and don't come back.
-Yeah.

18:53.400 --> 18:55.920
-Terrible.
-Get out of here.

18:56.000 --> 18:57.760
-Go away.
-What an asshole.

18:57.840 --> 18:59.720
-Look at him.
-Just go home.

18:59.800 --> 19:01.080
-Asshole.
-It's my vote.

19:01.160 --> 19:02.840
How could you do that?

19:02.920 --> 19:04.240
Why?

19:12.960 --> 19:14.960
To show my sincerity

19:17.240 --> 19:18.720
and take responsibility

19:19.680 --> 19:22.440
for selecting a corrupt team member,

19:26.000 --> 19:29.080
I hereby resign from my position
as student body president,

19:30.040 --> 19:33.240
effective immediately.

19:40.320 --> 19:42.400
What the hell is this?

19:51.880 --> 19:53.800
Why didn't you destroy the evidence?

19:55.640 --> 19:57.640
I didn't make a copy.

20:00.880 --> 20:02.400
Why didn't you expose me yourself?

20:03.280 --> 20:04.560
I just wanted to know

20:05.080 --> 20:08.800
whether you're really a hero or a villain.

20:13.480 --> 20:15.760
Haven't I already proven my innocence?

20:18.360 --> 20:20.120
By getting New expelled?

20:21.320 --> 20:23.360
That so-called "innocence"
is pretty brutal.

20:29.560 --> 20:30.800
I'll tell you something.

20:33.360 --> 20:35.600
Anyone who wants to go into politics

20:36.120 --> 20:38.160
must have a clean record.

20:38.760 --> 20:40.840
You can't afford stains like this.

20:42.040 --> 20:45.360
And besides, those who do wrong
should face the consequences.

20:46.440 --> 20:47.840
Isn't that fair?

20:49.000 --> 20:51.040
And what if you lose

20:51.920 --> 20:53.280
the next election?

20:56.440 --> 20:57.440
Remember this.

20:58.960 --> 21:00.320
People like me

21:01.400 --> 21:03.360
don't make the same mistake twice.

21:04.600 --> 21:08.440
Humans tend to repeat the same mistakes
over and over again

21:08.520 --> 21:12.040
until they die
or until they finally stop being foolish.

21:12.120 --> 21:13.280
That's not me!

21:15.360 --> 21:19.840
But most people die
before they stop being foolish.

21:21.720 --> 21:24.200
What makes you think
you'll be any different?

21:24.920 --> 21:27.280
Because you think
you're better than everyone else?

21:31.440 --> 21:32.680
That's exactly

21:34.000 --> 21:36.080
why I like you, Paradorn.

21:39.840 --> 21:41.520
Shall we find out

21:42.640 --> 21:45.600
what kind of person
you'll become in the future?

22:26.920 --> 22:28.000
HOMECOMING DAY

22:28.080 --> 22:30.640
OUTSTANDING ALUMNUS
MINISTER PARADORN TANGNAITHAM

22:31.920 --> 22:33.960
I would like to thank
the alumni association

22:34.040 --> 22:36.920
for granting me
this outstanding alumni award.

22:37.800 --> 22:39.280
As you all know,

22:40.120 --> 22:43.000
I first ran for election at this school.

22:43.640 --> 22:44.960
But it's more than that.

22:46.160 --> 22:51.760
Everything that made me
who I am today started here.

23:13.080 --> 23:13.920
Hey, hurry up.

23:15.240 --> 23:17.760
Take these three boxes out
and replace them.

23:19.440 --> 23:21.200
Hurry. What are you doing?

23:23.720 --> 23:24.560
If we get caught…

23:25.960 --> 23:27.760
How would you explain this, sir?

23:27.840 --> 23:29.520
Did you rig an election before?

23:29.600 --> 23:30.640
Please answer, sir.

23:30.720 --> 23:31.960
He's so fake.

23:32.040 --> 23:33.360
I shouldn't have believed him.

23:33.440 --> 23:35.400
I'm not voting for you anymore.

23:35.480 --> 23:36.840
-Yeah, me too.
-You asshole.

23:37.440 --> 23:40.000
That's not what happened.
Please listen to me.

23:40.080 --> 23:43.360
Hey, I did my best. I took responsibility.

23:43.440 --> 23:45.600
Please… I already took responsibility.

23:45.680 --> 23:46.880
Hey, listen to me.

23:46.960 --> 23:49.240
I already took responsibility.

23:49.320 --> 23:52.320
-Sir, answer us.
-What really happened?

23:52.400 --> 23:55.880
-That's enough. Excuse us.
-Answer us, sir.

23:55.960 --> 23:58.760
-Excuse us.
-Hey!

24:18.960 --> 24:20.840
Think again.

24:53.080 --> 24:54.360
Hey, hurry up.

24:54.440 --> 24:56.800
Take these three boxes out
and replace them.

25:16.880 --> 25:20.160
Hello, New.
Call everyone for an urgent meeting.

25:21.320 --> 25:26.560
I want us to start working on
the smart crosswalk project immediately.

25:38.840 --> 25:40.760
We finally won, Paradorn.

25:40.840 --> 25:42.160
Damn, this is amazing.

25:43.040 --> 25:44.600
I've been waiting for this day.

25:45.400 --> 25:47.400
ANNUAL POLICY: SMART CROSSWALK PROJECT

25:48.080 --> 25:49.520
Right, Paradorn?

25:51.360 --> 25:52.360
Paradorn.

25:57.520 --> 25:58.520
Hey, Paradorn.

26:49.920 --> 26:51.880
Are you okay?

27:06.320 --> 27:07.320
Nanno!

27:15.480 --> 27:16.480
Nanno!

27:19.720 --> 27:22.840
Tell me the truth. Is what I saw real?

27:24.840 --> 27:26.600
You don't have to believe it.

27:29.120 --> 27:32.280
Then delete that damn clip
right here in front of me.

27:34.720 --> 27:36.880
I said there's no copy.

27:36.960 --> 27:39.560
-So then there's no copy.
-You think I'm stupid?

27:40.760 --> 27:42.720
I don't need a copy.

27:51.080 --> 27:52.880
Because your wrongdoing

27:54.520 --> 27:55.680
goes far beyond that.

27:55.760 --> 27:58.480
Hey. I almost really got hit
by the car earlier.

27:58.560 --> 28:00.520
You should pay me more.

28:00.600 --> 28:02.480
We agreed on the price.
That's all you get.

28:02.560 --> 28:04.080
Why are you asking for more now?

28:04.160 --> 28:07.040
That accident where you became a hero

28:08.120 --> 28:10.640
was your doing too, wasn't it?

28:14.200 --> 28:15.960
Like I said,

28:16.040 --> 28:21.560
people keep making
the same stupid mistakes until they die.

29:16.120 --> 29:17.720
Some people,

29:18.240 --> 29:20.240
even when they stand in the light,

29:20.760 --> 29:22.800
let darkness consume them.

29:26.960 --> 29:28.680
But others,

29:29.240 --> 29:31.080
even when surrounded by darkness,

29:32.120 --> 29:35.360
refuse to let
their inner light be extinguished.

29:48.160 --> 29:49.280
Hey!

29:54.840 --> 29:55.960
Nanno.

30:03.920 --> 30:05.360
How did you get here?

30:08.640 --> 30:10.320
Shouldn't I be the one asking you?

32:43.240 --> 32:45.360
Honestly, I feel happier right now

32:45.440 --> 32:48.040
than I did
when I was appointed as a minister.

32:48.560 --> 32:50.280
As everyone knows,

32:50.360 --> 32:53.240
I first ran for election at this school.

32:53.920 --> 32:55.120
But it's more than that.

32:55.640 --> 33:01.080
Everything that made me
who I am today started here.

33:01.160 --> 33:03.360
HOMECOMING DAY
OUTSTANDING ALUMNUS

33:42.640 --> 33:44.880
A world that has been reset…

33:45.800 --> 33:50.680
I hope
there are still some good people left.

33:54.560 --> 33:58.160
See you again next semester, everyone.

